# LuxeMarket — Backend

FastAPI backend with PostgreSQL, Redis, and a scikit-learn valuation model.

## Requirements

- Python 3.12+
- Docker Desktop (for Postgres + Redis)

## Quickstart

```bash
# 1. Start infrastructure
make up

# 2. Create virtual environment
cd backend
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt

# 3. Run migrations
make migrate

# 4. Seed data
make seed

# 5. Compute valuations and deal scores
make valuate

# 6. Start dev server
make dev

# Open http://localhost:8000/docs
```

## Environment variables

Copy `.env.example` to `backend/.env`. Defaults work with Docker Compose.

| Variable | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `DATABASE_URL` | `postgresql://luxe:luxe_dev@localhost:5432/luxemarket` | Postgres connection string |
| `REDIS_URL` | `redis://localhost:6379` | Redis connection string |
| `APP_ENV` | `development` | Environment name |
| `SECRET_KEY` | `change_me_in_production` | App secret (change in prod!) |

## API

Swagger UI available at `http://localhost:8000/docs` when server is running.

| Endpoint | Description |
|---|---|
| `GET /api/v1/health` | Liveness check |
| `GET /api/v1/listings` | Paginated listings with filters |
| `GET /api/v1/listings/top-deals` | Listings with deal score > 60 |
| `GET /api/v1/listings/{id}` | Single listing with valuation |
| `GET /api/v1/makes` | All makes with listing counts |
| `GET /api/v1/makes/{make}/models` | Models for a specific make |
| `GET /api/v1/trends` | Market snapshots by make/model |
| `GET /api/v1/trends/summary` | Dashboard summary stats |

## Data pipeline
data/seeds/seed.py   →  Generates 1,500 mock listings  →  listings table
data/valuate.py      →  Ridge regression model         →  valuations + deal_scores tables
→  market_snapshots table

## Running tests

```bash
cd backend
source .venv/bin/activate
pytest tests/ -v
```